From: buntOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] soc: mediatek: add the MT6897 connectivity subsystem power driver

The connsys of the MT6897 powers its radios and an RF chip on an
internal SPI bus. Linux owns the PMIC rails, the pads of the interface
to the RF chip and the CONN power domain. The secure firmware does the
rest of the sequence on request, as SIP calls. The order here is that of
the stock driver, and the calls and their arguments have been compared
with it by a script.

This does not do everything the stock driver does:

 - The rails stay on in the normal mode while a radio is on, where the
   stock driver gives them to the SRCLKEN hardware request and the low
   power mode at the end of power on. That costs idle power, and it
   can't get a mode wrong.
 - There is no thermal query, power dump or debug path.
 - The clock type comes from the MT6685 only. The stock driver also knows
   of a TCXO configuration which this board does not have.

The bootloader writes the address of the firmware in the node of the
device in the boot modes where it loads the firmware, and not in
recovery or power-off charging. Without it the driver stops there, with
no rail on and no SIP call made. The platform code powers the CONN domain
around the probe either way.

The stock driver makes the first SIP call once per boot, and what a
second one does in the secure firmware isn't known. A module can be
loaded more than once in a boot, so this one stays loaded from that call
on.

Each step of a power on is logged, as a wrong step can hang the bus
without a word and the last line says where. It stays that way until the
driver has seen real use.
---
 drivers/soc/mediatek/Kconfig             |  14 +
 drivers/soc/mediatek/Makefile            |   1 +
 drivers/soc/mediatek/mtk-connsys.c       | 655 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 include/linux/soc/mediatek/mtk-connsys.h |  28 +
 4 files changed, 698 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/mediatek/Kconfig b/drivers/soc/mediatek/Kconfig
index d729397..488471c 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/mediatek/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/soc/mediatek/Kconfig
@@ -17,6 +17,20 @@ config MTK_CMDQ
 	  time limitation, such as updating display configuration during the
 	  vblank.
 
+config MTK_CONNSYS
+	tristate "MediaTek connectivity subsystem base power driver"
+	depends on ARCH_MEDIATEK || COMPILE_TEST
+	depends on ARM64 && HAVE_ARM_SMCCC
+	depends on OF && REGULATOR && SPMI
+	depends on PINCTRL
+	select REGMAP
+	help
+	  Say yes here to add support for the base part of the connectivity
+	  subsystem of the MediaTek MT6897. It powers the Wi-Fi and Bluetooth
+	  radios of the SoC and their RF chip, with the help of the secure
+	  firmware, and tells the radio drivers where the bootloader has put
+	  their firmware.
+
 config MTK_DEVAPC
 	tristate "Mediatek Device APC Support"
 	help
diff --git a/drivers/soc/mediatek/Makefile b/drivers/soc/mediatek/Makefile
index 0665573..6f38c34 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/mediatek/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/soc/mediatek/Makefile
@@ -1,5 +1,6 @@
 # SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
 obj-$(CONFIG_MTK_CMDQ) += mtk-cmdq-helper.o
+obj-$(CONFIG_MTK_CONNSYS) += mtk-connsys.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_MTK_DEVAPC) += mtk-devapc.o
